ened in the books  we needed the crew to split up we needed  amos and naomi  to face their past those things more or  less are progressing on their normal  path  we needed alex and bobby to team up so  that we could get an idea about what was  happening on mars  the seeds of the lakonian empire being  planted there  we needed avasarala to be put in charge  of earth  in the aftermath of the attacks we  needed holden to be isolated somewhat so  that he could grow as a character  and game-wise it has to make sense that  he'll turn down the role of the head of  the transport  union when it's offered to him books one  through four holden probably wouldn't  have done that  earth has to start dying marco needs to  make his case for the free navy  and there needs to be some pushback  against that as far as changes  fred dying early is one of the big ones  it seems surprising to me because  there's this void now  in the regular opa or the moderate wing  whatever you want to refer to them as  how he dies isn't terribly important i  mean it was nice to see someone die in a  high g maneuver just to show that that  is a thing that can happen  story wise it does change things some  the three characters at the center of  the taiko story don't really have the  opa connections that fred did  bull's an unknown he's basically taking  the place a book drummer  and the fact that he's an earther makes  it pretty unlikely he'd step in to take  fred's place  for monica it's the same and i guess you  could imagine a way that holden just  steps into that role  he's well known to belters in the same  way that fred johnson was when he first  came on the scene  but fred had anderson dawes behind him  which brings up the question  what is dawes up to are they still gonna  do fred's funeral  that's so out of whack with the timeline  it's hard to say  personally i'd be pretty surprised if  jared harris showed up to reprise the  role at this point in the story  for one they would have had to keep it a  complete secret there's been no talk of  that whatsoever  and it also seems unlikely because he's  working on the apple plus series for  foundation and work for both series  would have been going on around the same  time  so i'm interested in hearing your  thoughts on what happens in fred's  absence  the other idea i hear a lot is that  drummer is going to come and take his  place but that  all hinges on how much of michiopaw's  role she's taking on this season  based just off of what we've seen in  season five it looks like she's just  michio paw  she'll join the free navy and then  she'll follow marco until she doesn't  one of the things that makes that seem a  little less likely is  michio's motivations in the book  compared to where drummer's at  they both kind of went independent for  the same reasons  but they gave drummer this close  relationship with ashford  joe ashford is obviously a much more  likable character  and she did have a connection with him  and even though she had a falling out  with fred  she still respects him michio didn't  like either of them so i could kind of  see it going both ways i could kind of  see her looking at things pragmatically  and then joining the free navy because  it makes the most sense for her family  but with things how they are the fact  that marco killed two people that she  cares about i could also see a split in  her faction  because at this point at least it seems  that some of them are sympathetic to  what the free navy are trying to do  and none of them at this point seem to  have the same connection with fred  johnson  or ashford overall i do think by the end  of season six she will be in michio's  role  as far as becoming the leader of the  transport union  this will change book drummers the  original drummer's  importance later on but i think that  carragee is such a fan favorite and this  character has become such a big part of  what's going on in the belt i think it  makes for a more satisfying ending  to have her be there for that it could  just be an easter egg but i find it a  little bit interesting that they named  one of her wives michio  and that does make me think that maybe  there will be a split  but at the same time i can't see them  building up that character  who so far isn't really even the most  important of the people on her  ship to have this really exciting pirate  queen  redemption arc kind of thing that michio  does  but i'm interested to hear what you guys  are thinking about that  as far as other changes i think most of  what we've seen in naomi's story are  just details  they change the details around how she  got to the pella  how she contacted holden about the rossi  i think mostly it's still going in the  same direction  i think most of those are just changes  out of necessity they're not able to  show us what she's thinking we don't get  that great insight to how she figures  out her plan  as her time on the pella passes i think  philip will try to bring her over to  marco's  side sin is already doing that he'll  continue to do that but i think for the  whole thing to work at the end  her setting it up so that the free navy  go dutchman  i think for that to have the weight that  it does she has to believe that philip  might  be on the ship at that time so i don't  see any major changes in his story  and i don't think any of the changes  we've seen in season 5 so far  hinted any major changes in naomi's  story speaking of going dutchmen  i get a lot of questions about the high  council and the fact that they use  soviet terror as the contact point  rather than  duarte himself during alex and bobby's  investigation  i think as far as sovietteres concerned  i don't think he's a replacement for  duarte  i think his ending will be exactly the  same i think that we'll see him go  dutchman  i think maybe they just introduced him  early so we know who he is when we see  that happen  if you remember reading the book the  first time in the epilogue 